data purging, and lock updates, ensuring the correct cross-device unlocking flow in `index.html`. Existing test scripts, including auto-record gating, stealth mask, and hardened checks, must remain operational.\n\nReviewing the post-clear-students feedback, the display state of `#sub-feed` requires clarification. The previous silent operation had its own feedback with `#reset-status-msg` which is no longer applicable. The current design leaves feedback stale. The question becomes how much and what feedback is useful: should `#sub-feed` be updated to reflect the lock reset, or remain as \"No records saved yet,\" or something else?\n\n\nThe current design's modal feedback, specifically within `#sub-feed`, poses a challenge. Any manual text inserted there would be overwritten by `refreshSubmissions()` within seconds. A direct approach is to use the existing `refreshSubmissions()` to handle feedback, simplifying the process and avoiding visual glitches, such as an optional `#sub-status-msg`. This keeps `#view-sub` cleaner and improves the cross-device behavior of `Clear Students`.\n\nThe confirmation modal's wording and styling in `tmp_backup/teacher.html` requires evaluation. The current text \"Are you sure this is what you want?\" is not explicit enough for the combined action. The updated warning must explicitly alert the user to the combined action to clear submissions AND reset the response lock.\n\n\nThe confirmation modal's text must explicitly state the combined action: clearing students also resets the response lock. Replacing the modal heading with a clear, concise message achieves this. The plan is to create a well-formatted message within `implementation_plan.md` to get user approval before making any code changes.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_file","args":{"ArtifactMetadata":"{\"RequestFeedback\":true,\"Summary\":\"Implementation plan to remove the Reset tab in teacher.html, combine lockEpoch reset with Clear Students via concurrent Promise.all(purgeRecords, patchField), update the confirmation modal warning, and verify all affected flows.\",\"UserFacing\":true}","Content":"\"# Implementation Plan — Combine Lock Reset with Clear Students & Remove Reset Tab (`Patch 1.0.24`)\\n\\n## Investigation Summary & Architectural Analysis\\n1. **Current State in `teacher.html`:**\\n   - Top navigation (`<nav class=\\\"tab-nav\\\">`) currently has 3 tabs: `Quiz Editor` (`#tab-btn-editor`), `Submissions` (`#tab-btn-sub`), and `Reset` (`#tab-btn-reset` -> `#view-reset` with `#reset-lock-btn` & `#reset-status-msg`).\\n   - `#clear-sub-btn` (`Clear Students`) and `#reset-lock-btn` share `#confirm-modal` via a `pendingAction` state variable (`'clearSub'` vs `'resetLock'`), running `EncryptedLocalDB.purgeRecords(quizId)` and `EncryptedLocalDB.patchField(quizId, 'lockEpoch', nextEpoch)` separately.\\n   - Because `Patch 1.0.23` hides `#clear-sub-btn` whenever `Auto Record Quiz` (`settingsState.autoRecordQuiz`) is `false`, combining lock reset into `#clear-sub-btn` means lock resets via UI will only be visible when `Auto Record Quiz` is `ON`.\\n2. **Current State in `index.html`:**\\n   - Student devices check `checkRemoteUnlock(data)` against `quizzes/{quizId}.lockEpoch` on load (live REST and `#local-db-vault` fallback). Because `index.html` depends solely on `lockEpoch`, **no changes are needed in `index.html`** or `quizzes/template`.\\n\\n## Research & Optimization Rationale\\n- **Concurrent Execution (`Promise.all`):** Using `Promise.all([EncryptedLocalDB.purgeRecords(quizId), EncryptedLocalDB.patchField(quizId, 'lockEpoch', nextEpoch)])` executes submission deletion (`<= 500` batch commits) and the `lockEpoch` masked `PATCH` in parallel in one round-trip window instead of sequentially. Unlike packing them into a single `:commit` payload, reusing `purgeRecords()` + `patchField()` keeps zero duplicated Firestore `:commit` serialization code (DRY), continues handling `>500` submissions cleanly, and still bumps `lockEpoch` even when `0` submission docs exist.\\n- **UI & State Simplification:** Removing `#tab-btn-reset`, `#view-reset`, `#reset-lock-btn`, `#reset-status-msg`, and `pendingAction` eliminates dead DOM no\n<truncated 4459 bytes>","Overwrite":"true","Path":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\CxAdmin\\\\.gemini\\\\antigravity\\\\brain\\\\8f2bd4b5-d81b-4839-aa40-a5c3a5acaa6a\\\\implementation_plan.md\""}}],"truncated_fields":["thinking","tool_calls"]}
