{"step_index":1269,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-10T21:49:25Z","content":"Created At: 2026-11-11T05:49:25+08:00\nCompleted At: 2026-11-11T05:49:33+08:00\nCreated At: 2026-11-11T05:49:25+08:00\nCompleted At: 2026-11-11T05:49:33+08:00\nThe search for \"Firestore REST API list collection query documents orderBy mask fields vanilla JS\" returned the following summary:\nTo query a collection using the **Cloud Firestore REST API** with Vanilla JavaScript (`fetch`), you need to use the `runQuery` endpoint via a **`POST`** request[1][2]. \n\nTo accomplish **filtering fields (Mask/Projection)**, **ordering (`orderBy`)**, and targeting a collection, you construct a `structuredQuery` object in the request body[3][4][5].\n\n### Vanilla JavaScript Example\n\n```javascript\nasync function queryFirestoreDocuments() {\n  const projectId = \"YOUR_PROJECT_ID\";\n  const databaseId = \"(default)\"; // usually (default)\n  const collectionName = \"users\"; // your collection\n  \n  // Optional: If your Firestore rules require authentication, pass a Bearer token\n  const authToken = \"YOUR_FIREBASE_AUTH_TOKEN\"; \n\n  // Endpoint for running structured queries\n  const url = `https://firestore.googleapis.com/v1/projects/${projectId}/databases/${databaseId}/documents:runQuery`;\n\n  // Construct the Structured Query payload\n  const requestBody = {\n    structuredQuery: {\n      // 1. Specify the collection to query\n      from: [{ collectionId: collectionName }],\n\n      // 2. Mask/Projection: Return only specific fields to reduce payload size\n      select: {\n        fields: [\n          { fieldPath: \"fullName\" },\n          { fieldPath: \"email\" }\n        ]\n      },\n\n      // 3. Order results by a specific field\n      orderBy: [\n        {\n          field: { fieldPath: \"fullName\" },\n          direction: \"ASCENDING\" // or \"DESCENDING\"\n        }\n      ],\n\n      // Optional: Limit number of results\n      limit: 10\n    }\n  };\n\n  try {\n    const response = await fetch(url, {\n      method: \"POST\",\n      headers: {\n        \"Content-Type\": \"application/json\",\n        // \"Authorization\": `Bearer ${authToken}` // Uncomment if auth is needed\n      },\n      \n<truncated 1276 bytes>\n Ensure you have matching indexes created in your Firebase Console if sorting combined with inequality filters.*\n4. **Response Format**: Firestore returns an array of objects[1]. Each matched document is wrapped inside an object (`item.document`), containing the raw typed values (e.g., `stringValue`, `integerValue`, `booleanValue`).\n\nSources:\n[1] [google.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQEObZOD5mwY73zDEk_wz9_4MDSO-9AIwCxMys45weuAeWOv0tDYN4P_MatEVuYpUgBNbCkAX2jYSSNS56HAPys0GlQxNOh1jwNjq5KGP4i4BOGQT0awujvkEZ4kQFrgE9odj-AMdH9XyjCp5gYMvQ8bVrhTYGY28WEWprzAogXg6ufRwSphUEz0w_KaV0MWpwUilSpiAbRldWTF__n3)\n[2] [gitbook.io](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQEXO2i_3ah7hISJJXhwlpjx9Ba-FMkEHCDMfExW7uYRL4jGBBGQDgwvDSUh1MQXcT72IHKZLT8Iaryucxu0U027YajNgYY-yib0UBwe3WGzfH5JPedy_v9hJ0EsWQgHY7UoNkzF1CMAomJDF58z)\n[3] [google.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHwlTbSj0_jsGJO2HqgkMFoUQWZjTYvbC2asuWoJKKXByDYECe5k4itfiODqjH0c2WYBhHQi-9RfRQU7yFYtzlZ60C-FVeRjjMti2PdK5-TP5lQ2JprsPqGgYdDNtbHmrtLFKpLsKjUY1sqnIrh-rXOnNXiKcdblMquF3TwZo0BN4KPLH-pmJw=)\n[4] [google.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHrhEu2rAv201NTfL49vZsRJLmKUv4Pc_90Eqly3ue3VxrFJr15V_XCGaY9jSgplbUziGb3uVkTPhclHV-gTEP9jwjmknz_WK44HJvK75-NJ6FXlO6obf4yPAhBcDwNVP06PohxcNleJF79EaZYTRXJX3GQVRbhhvtwzg-6YO30eBwO)\n[5] [gitbook.io](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQEXO2i_3ah7hISJJXhwlpjx9Ba-FMkEHCDMfExW7uYRL4jGBBGQDgwvDSUh1MQXcT72IHKZLT8Iaryucxu0U027YajNgYY-yib0UBwe3WGzfH5JPedy_v9hJ0EsWQgHY7UoNkzF1CMAomJDF58z)\n[6] [stackoverflow.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQEG646nMctsNqrsKcqRoWyFIHTDYC7n74qhUTJpnROd-d_94eC50kWsV9vn3_Dlbvq50q_IijvHS1aHSgARSbSxcUmiEVAEF92GHK526J9agzQInWG3EWMQCSprkgWOoLGhJVeJLP2l3Pk55ImCymmzbLIHTsCX-iHg-x9m1kPEmLsbXdMXIXxwgwqavubhLuxFCRVscxa6bEd52mXZycCxwadn)\n\nNote: Source URLs are HTTP redirects; check where they resolve if you need the direct link.","truncated_fields":["content"]}
{"step_index":1270,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-10T21:49:25Z","content":"Created At: 2026-11-11T05:49:25+08:00\nCompleted At: 2026-11-11T05:49:37+08:00\nCreated At: 2026-11-11T05:49:25+08:00\nCompleted At: 2026-11-11T05:49:37+08:00\nThe search for \"HTML5 anchor download filename sanitization Windows reserved characters vanilla JS\" returned the following summary:\nWhen building client-side file downloads using vanilla JavaScript and the HTML5 `download` attribute (`<a href=\"...\" download=\"filename\">`), user-provided or dynamically generated strings can easily break downloads or cause security issues on Windows machines[1][2]. \n\nWindows file systems disallow specific **reserved characters**, **control codes**, **device names** (like `CON`, `NUL`, `COM1`), and **trailing periods/spaces**[3][4][5].\n\nHere is a robust, production-ready vanilla JavaScript helper function to thoroughly sanitize filenames for cross-platform safety (with a heavy focus on Windows limitations):\n\n### Vanilla JS Sanitization Function\n\n```javascript\nfunction sanitizeFilename(input, replacement = '_') {\n  if (typeof input !== 'string') return 'download';\n\n  // 1. Control characters (0x00–0x1f and 0x80–0x9f)\n  const controlRe = /[\\x00-\\x1f\\x80-\\x9f]/g;\n  \n  // 2. Windows reserved characters: < > : \" / \\ | ? *\n  const reservedCharsRe = /[<>:\"/\\\\|?*]/g;\n  \n  // 3. Windows reserved device names (CON, PRN, AUX, NUL, COM1-9, LPT1-9) with optional extension\n  const windowsReservedRe = /^(con|prn|aux|nul|com[1-9]|lpt[1-9])(\\..*)?$/i;\n  \n  // 4. Unix hidden files or relative paths if stripped poorly (optional safeguard for just dots)\n  const leadingTrailingDotsSpacesRe = /^[. ]+|[. ]+$/g;\n\n  let sanitized = input\n    .replace(controlRe, replacement)\n    .replace(reservedCharsRe, replacement)\n    .trim();\n\n  // Handle Windows reserved device names by prefixing them if matched\n  if (windowsReservedRe.test(sanitized)) {\n    sanitized = replacement + sanitized;\n  }\n\n  // Strip leading/trailing dots and spaces (Windows drops/malfunctions with these)\n  sanitized = sanitized.replace(leadingTrailingDotsSpacesRe, '');\n\n  // Fallback if\n<truncated 1796 bytes>\nt the file write[3][4].\n4. **Trailing/Leading Spaces & Periods:** Prevents file creation glitches on NTFS formatting by stripping edge spaces and dots (`.`)[4][5].\n5. **Length Restriction:** Caps the filename at 255 characters to abide by standard OS file system limits[3][4].\n\nSources:\n[1] [stackoverflow.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFhfX5agtYz6IQB7Go6i9d24SrWBcOOp2cCYtI4xVxUXXMKO9FEoscMZ6hfrg83XuBKPTly5gCOCRkmR9DVW_IrJUTsisPYPCcf-YgXCR8CRVmpfX-ZR_OakhyqQjMd8XOR0Sw94Db8R7pZWktGra6BDGpKt7zpX-iAy-uid361OPvbZQw58izNOiVfISwlrxWi)\n[2] [jonathancrozier.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGzwfh9fP7osDoYPt8-t4iyKLExbegUDyVVmgP-jk5OsG7f-FG00xp-VQN3q80a1d6_95eFhBpJL7NIuXCl3VSNOp0M5ZSjWgbEsLJfnbu_bX6srVb-2UhptQtdMMNOWoRJFYfaHTBDeQn4ppC6JQ21zpTPotwmm6PmmaxpOldpSORE7oa3uXlOA64_5SC0FTZYLdvCU3I=)\n[3] [github.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGqBgmrtaIeQXYGwiOJZWJbMbk1lOxFbArkHunV9FX8tl1P3BizFx2NZZJT5_hNeSMHHSvICMnN8nX3HLacuC_ZVtC-t7K-WmwhWwbwsCX-xHEf1IjFRdVAYCv6kXyfxdHuOw==)\n[4] [npmjs.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFSbQ24hWkZTn_Z5YhIitFbedqPauLujO3rgVd2spIgKKe_5TxSuqUpqT1Z544ttiHGp9WtYatp8Sf8ysvkF89Q1NFFVkh6vOBC0R0ZxkEVuVuh1E191g52jMOZSMiMptzcMAQv8Q==)\n[5] [stackoverflow.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFHHcvJD7-r019AXEdogV_bWYnDTSrgpeyOB64ID7dFZEIL3lfSvCGLk6ga19TRJrtQ1SjWMKyV3Q4jzgnSRfSbNKA82C2odd6Db97XhqWF1iTOB9vcAMJLt51uUPjOqmcu1tKOPbaxDwrD5G-t4kvFS4SqLqaOKGKNRsuznTkxX3I4WHgLg6hg8C-8GQLYpBwka4kOYDaekhU4maAjGsHyP3yCbA==)\n[6] [stackoverflow.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQEcwjZ_fYadyY1yRF0yL0zmKPufSQVapmI2diS1T62V33hAFrMW07zmXuw-9LUBcITfmy5wxrBuBAWuGAD1MPiLixbwlmGEZjYwV6XeysMpA-aGJkLiDHgskw-VROUXxhSw4dtaK5rq9wKMRbalsZC054npujlpm7kwRXoKZGLJTs3NSeyOTlf_aSm_VT0fcW3zXF1J5r7ojLE-y_3mrjyio1-Qub2a)\n\nNote: Source URLs are HTTP redirects; check where they resolve if you need the direct link.","truncated_fields":["content"]}
